					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/5150wned" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5175695); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5175695&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200703" alt="5150wned" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5175695)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/5150wned" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5175695); return false;" >5150wned</a></span> <span class="odate time_1568000647 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Sep 2019 03:44</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4356370">
									

<p>I wound up skimming. I came backwards through parts to see if I missed anything, and nope.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>One problem for me is that it is a character piece about a collective anomaly, and that's not really realized.</p>
<p>The conprocs don't make sense, there's a ban on electronics and metals, but there's no clear reason why this is the case. The masks, where are they stored? Separately? Why is a prismatic shaft required, what would be wrong with a viewing window?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>ferromagnetic charge</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Makes me hurt&#8230; you're throwing in sciencey sounding words to add weight but you're using them wrong.</p>
<p>It's just that the containment is leading me to believe that there's some real need for all of it&#8230; and there isn't. That's my major dislike here.</p>
<p>Some nitpicks:<br />
Footnote 2 is a bit redundant.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>but since the discovery of SCP-4064's emotional properties, it has been lifted from his record.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Breaks suspension that SCP would do this, either the dr. wouldn't be punished in the first place (suspended pending review, for example) or the reprimand would stick (SCP doesn't care if it was cause an anomaly got you, it just means you f*ked up to let it happen).</p>
<p>The interviews and addenda just don't hit me hard at all. The conprocs had me looking right and the narrative was turning left.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
-1
							</div>

								
					
